    "A8": {
      "worksheet": "UK electricity",
      "xmlPath": "xl/worksheets/sheet10.xml",
      "cell": "A8",
      "value": "UK electricity conversion factors should be used to report on electricity used by an organisation at sites owned/controlled by them.  This is reported as a Scope 2, indirect emission.  The conversion factors in this listing are for the electricity supplied to the grid that organisations purchase - they do not include the emissions associated with the transmission and distribution of electricity.",
      "rawValue": "647",
      "type": "s",
      "numberFormat": "General",
      "styleId": 448,
      "formula": null
    },
    "A12": {
      "worksheet": "UK electricity",
      "xmlPath": "xl/worksheets/sheet10.xml",
      "cell": "A12",
      "value": "●  The Government's 'Environmental reporting guidelines' require that Scope 2 electricity emissions are reported using location-based grid average emissions factors. A market-based Scope 2 figure may optionally be reported but only in addition to the location-based figure. Market-based emissions reflect a contractual entitlement to claim an emissions rate, allowing for a reduced emission figure where, for example, a renewable energy tariff is backed by certificates to track attributes associated with energy generation. The location-based emissions reflect the average emission of the grid where the energy consumption occurs and is calculated using these UK Electricity grid average factors below. Organisations using a market-based figure may want to consider adding narrative information on whether their contractual arrangements cause additional renewable electricity generation.",
      "rawValue": "649",
      "type": "s",
      "numberFormat": "General",
      "styleId": 451,
      "formula": null
    },
    "A22": {
      "worksheet": "UK electricity",
      "xmlPath": "xl/worksheets/sheet10.xml",
      "cell": "A22",
      "value": "The kWh electricity use is multiplied by the ‘electricity generated’ figure appropriate to the reporting year to produce company G's UK Scope 2 electricity emissions.",
      "rawValue": "657",
      "type": "s",
      "numberFormat": "General",
      "styleId": 447,
